                <pb facs="0229" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.76/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Greece</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Goold</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-03T17:00:00-04:00">May 3, 1929—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>21. Your 34, May 2, 5 p.m. Department approves of request made in your letter to
                    Mr. Venizelos and wishes you to continue to accord every appropriate assistance
                    in this matter.</p>
                <p>Please keep Department promptly informed of further developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
